WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
[Light café jazz plays. A dog wearing fake cat ears
approaches a robot at a CATS ONLY club.] Dog: Meow?

00:06.000 --> 00:10.000
[Forward pass: the robot makes a prediction.]
Robot: Pointy ears. Definitely a cat!

00:10.000 --> 00:13.000
[The robot stamps APPROVED and lets the dog in.]

00:13.000 --> 00:16.400
[Compare: the prediction meets the correct label.]
Dog: WOOF!

00:16.400 --> 00:18.400
Cat manager: That… is a dog.

00:18.400 --> 00:21.000
Robot: Oh.

00:21.000 --> 00:26.000
[Backpropagation: a correction signal travels backward.]
Robot: I relied too much on the ears.

00:26.000 --> 00:33.000
[The diagram traces how the settings contributed
to the mistake. No settings have changed yet.]

00:33.000 --> 00:38.500
[Update: the settings begin to change.]
Cat manager: More examples. Keep practicing.

00:38.500 --> 00:44.000
Robot: Adjust. Try again.
[Sliders for ears, other clues, and bias are adjusted.]

00:44.000 --> 00:48.000
[Later: the dog returns with even bigger fake cat ears.]
Dog: Meow?

00:48.000 --> 00:51.500
Robot: Nice try.

00:51.500 --> 00:54.700
Dog: …Meow?
[The cat looks unimpressed. The camera moves to “…”.]

00:54.700 --> 00:57.700
[An awkward pause. Only “…” remains. Jazz continues.]

00:57.700 --> 01:00.200
by Dr. Chi-Ning (Nick) Chang
Music: Good Morning Café Jazz — sleepvolume, Pixabay.

01:00.200 --> 01:01.000
[The music ends. The picture fades to black.]
